at="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TANAKA, JUNJI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ARAI SUSUMU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>EGUCHI TOSHIMASA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TANAKA JUNJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ARAI, SUSUMU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>EGUCHI, TOSHIMASA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TANAKA, JUNJI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A continuous production method for a thermoplastic polymer sheet excellent in surface smoothness and small in planar retardation, that is, small in optical phase difference and in warpage, wherein a thermoplastic polymer sheet molten-extruded from a T-die or coat hanger die is formed into a cooled sheet by using a metal belt having a maximum surface roughness (Rmax) of up to 0.1  mu m and a length for permitting at least 20-second, curvature-free contact in a feeding direction of the thermoplastic polymer sheet extruded from the die.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette invention concerne un procédé de fabrication en continu de feuille polymère thermoplastique caractérisée par un excellent lissé de surface, une faible différence de phase optique et un faible voilage. Après extrusion en fusion à partir d'une matrice en T, la feuille polymère thermoplastique est refroidie au moyen d'une courroie métallique d'une rugosité de surface maxi (Rmax) de 0,1  mu m et d'une longueur suffisante pour autoriser un contact d'au moins 20 secondes, sans courbure dans le sens d'alimentation de la feuille polymère thermoplastique depuis sa sortie de la matrice.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>